  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-10T21:27:45.740Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When using TeleportTo to force rotate a player, a hitch appears whenever the player looks up to ~330 degrees and down to ~30 degrees, these numbers being dependent on the avatar in some way.\n\nWhat is noticeable is that the IK changes when the hitch occurs, arms being straightened and spine moving, however even with movement animations turned off it happens.\n\nThe faster the rotation, the larger the hitch is.\n\nI have a video showing off what happens https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dwoCjBpWX44 \n\nThe most interesting part being that when I bring up the debug menu in the latter part of the video, you can see the \"AngularY\" briefly turning negative.",
